          "grounding_supports": [
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                1
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 322,
                "end_index": 652,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Intel CPU Instability & Degradation Scandal (2024\u2013Present)\nIn the tech and gaming communities, \"IntelGate\" is the colloquial term for a major hardware crisis surrounding Intel's **13th and 14th Generation Core desktop processors** (codenamed \"Raptor Lake\" and \"Raptor Lake Refresh,\" such as the Core i9-13900K and i9-14900K)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 675,
                "end_index": 835,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Starting in late 2023 and peaking in mid-2024, desktop users, PC builders, and enterprise game-server providers began reporting massive, non-stop system crashes"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                2
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 837,
                "end_index": 1020,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Computers would crash to the desktop, throw mysterious \"out of video memory\" errors during game loading screens (even on high-end GPUs), or suffer from the Blue Screen of Death (BSOD)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1024,
                "end_index": 1170,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Initially, Intel tried to deflect the blame onto motherboard manufacturers, arguing their default BIOS profiles pushed too much power to the chips"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1172,
                "end_index": 1312,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "However, investigative tech journalists (most notably *Gamers Nexus* and *Level1Techs*) proved that the processors were physically degrading"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1409,
                "end_index": 1662,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**Vmin Shift Instability (The Microcode Bug):** Intel's own microcode algorithm had a bug that caused the CPU to request excessively high voltages (over-volting) during various operational states, even when the computer was idle or under light workloads"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1664,
                "end_index": 1838,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Over time, this excessive electrical pressure physically degraded the clock tree circuits inside the processor, causing permanent, irreversible physical damage to the silicon"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1843,
                "end_index": 2070,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "**Via Oxidation:** A separate manufacturing defect from late 2022/early 2023 caused some early batches of 13th Gen processors to experience chemical oxidation of the silicon vias, causing the chips to decay and fail prematurely"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                1,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2074,
                "end_index": 2190,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### The Resolution\nOnce a CPU is physically degraded, no software patch can fix it\u2014it must be physically replaced"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10,
                11
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2192,
                "end_index": 2417,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "To address the scandal, Intel:\n* **Extended Warranties:** Extended the manufacturer's warranty by an additional two years for all boxed and tray 13th and 14th Gen processors, allowing affected users to get replacements (RMAs)"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7,
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2419,
                "end_index": 2640,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Released Microcode Patches:** Delivered sequential BIOS updates (including 0x129, 0x12B, and later 0x12F) to motherboard manufacturers to permanently cap voltage limits and protect processors that had not yet degraded"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2642,
                "end_index": 2759,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Enforced Default Settings:** Mandated motherboard manufacturers use safer \"Intel Default Settings\" out of the box"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2774,
                "end_index": 3006,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The CENTCOM Intelligence Manipulation Scandal (2015)\nIn political and military contexts, \"Intelgate\" refers to a 2015 scandal inside the United States military's Central Command (CENTCOM) regarding the politicization of intelligence"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3029,
                "end_index": 3193,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In mid-2015, more than 50 intelligence analysts working for CENTCOM blew the whistle, filing a formal complaint with the Department of Defense\u2019s Inspector General"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                13
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3197,
                "end_index": 3386,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The analysts accused senior military officials of systematically altering, \"cooking,\" and sanitizing intelligence reports concerning the threat of ISIS (the Islamic State) in Iraq and Syria"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3390,
                "end_index": 3587,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "#### The Controversy\nAccording to the whistleblowers, senior leaders modified the analysts' raw intelligence to paint an overly optimistic picture of the U.S.-led coalition\u2019s efforts against ISIS"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3589,
                "end_index": 3739,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Reports were allegedly altered to make it appear that ISIS was weaker and that the U.S. military campaign was far more successful than it actually was"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14,
                15
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3741,
                "end_index": 3884,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The analysts claimed they faced professional pressure to conform their findings to the Obama administration\u2019s public, more positive narrative"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                16
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3983,
                "end_index": 4289,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In early 2017, the IG concluded that while there were deep communication breakdowns, a highly dysfunctional command climate, and distinct process errors, the allegations that senior leaders *intentionally* altered or suppressed intelligence to mislead the public or Congress were \"largely unsubstantiated.\""
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                14
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 3983,
                "end_index": 4432,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "In early 2017, the IG concluded that while there were deep communication breakdowns, a highly dysfunctional command climate, and distinct process errors, the allegations that senior leaders *intentionally* altered or suppressed intelligence to mislead the public or Congress were \"largely unsubstantiated.\" Nonetheless, the scandal sparked massive congressional hearings and reform in how intelligence is processed within regional combatant commands"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            }
          ],
